# Run, Jump, Flag

A one-screen browser game: a square runs and jumps over a gap to reach a flag. Everything is in `index.html` (inline JavaScript, no dependencies).

## Start
Open `index.html` in a browser (or a headless one). Releases `build-1`, `build-2` carry the same file as an asset.

## Controls
| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Left / Right or A / D | run |
| Space / Up / W | jump |
| R | restart (keeps the fall counter) |

Falling into the gap respawns you at the start. Touching the flag wins.

## Smoke test
`smoke.mjs` drives the game in headless Chromium: start, run right and left, jump, cross the gap, reach the flag. It exits non-zero on any failure.

```
npm i playwright && npx playwright install chromium
node smoke.mjs [index.html]
```
(Set `PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` to a playwright `index.mjs` if it is installed elsewhere.)

The game exposes `window.__game.state` (`x`, `y`, `onGround`, `won`, `deaths`, ...) for tests.
